*L_00300:
	@L_0007f:
*L_00305:
	ZH 1:
	'Important events can be triggered through the Harem'
	R
	'and Talk commands. Collecting a levy from a city'
	R
	'may also trigger events in that city.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'I would highly recommend not looking at guides for'
	R
	'your first playthrough and to accept your losses.'
	R
	'Failure is part of the game.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_00344:
	ZH 1:
	'Treasures may be bought from Pluepet, plundered from'
	R
	'cities or found in dungeons. When you select'
	R
	'\"Treasure\" on the main menu, a list is displayed.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Some treasures can be equipped. If you want to'
	R
	'equip one, select it, then select the character'
	R
	'you wish to equip it to.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_00383:
	ZH 1:
	'The game will be automatically saved at the'
	R
	'beginning of each turn to an auto-save slot.'
	R
	'Loaded data will also overwrite the auto-save slot.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'You can manually save data as well. Regardless of'
	R
	'when you save during a turn, however, when you load'
	R
	'that data you’ll be at the beginning of that turn.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_003c2:
	ZH 1:
	'HP: The general’s current HP. (die if it hits 0)'
	R
	'Attack/Defense: General’s battle capabilities.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Strategic Ability, Successful Strategy Chance:'
	R
	'The general with the highest chance, whether enemy'
	R
	'or ally, gets the opportunity to execute a strategy.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'If you successfully execute a strategy, you’ll gain'
	R
	'a great advantage during battle.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Situational Command Ability:'
	R
	'A value that’s added to the general and troops in'
	R
	'a unit’s stats depending on the type of battle.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'All generals have unique advantages and'
	R
	'disadvantages, so you should pay attention to these'
	R
	'and use each general when appropriate.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Troops:'
	R
	'All generals lead a specific type of troop with its'
	R
	'own attack and defense.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Special Attacks:'
	R
	'Some generals have special attacks that are usable'
	R
	'after waiting once. They have a variety of effects.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_00484:
	ZH 1:
	'When you attack, a number indicating the number of'
	R
	'troops attacking will fly at the target of the'
	R
	'attack, then become the number of enemies defeated.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'For example, if the number 1000 flies to the enemy'
	R
	'troops and becomes 200, it means 1000 troops'
	R
	'attacked and killed 200 enemies.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Depending on the situation, the general may attack'
	R
	'or be directly attacked. Unlike each troop that'
	R
	'attacks one time, a general may attack many times.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'If a general is killed, however, then the entire'
	R
	'unit is wiped out regardless of the number of'
	R
	'troops remaining.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'A general can attack and be attacked when their'
	R
	'number of troops is lower than the battle area.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_00513:
	ZH 1:
	'When a character’s turn comes, if they can attack,'
	R
	'left click the enemy you wish for them to attack.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'If you right click, a menu will appear with the'
	R
	'following commands.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Defend: Slightly raise defense for that turn.'
	R
	'Wait: Charges a special attack for some characters.'
	R
	'Retreat: Whole army retreats, resulting in a loss.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Auto-Attack: Unit keeps attacking front enemy.'
	R
	'Auto-Defend: Unit keeps defending.'
	R
	'Info: Display info of the unit right-clicked on.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'If a unit uses ranged or magic attacks, you can'
	R
	'also choose to make them direct attack in the right'
	R
	'click menu.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_0059b:
	ZH 1:
	'You can generally fight with a maximum of 4 units.'
	R
	'If you retreat or get wiped out, you lose. If you’re'
	R
	'attacking, running out of turns is also a loss.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Battle Turns:'
	R
	'You get a randomly decided number of approximately'
	R
	'4 turns. The battle ends when turns run out.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Certain battles may have no turn limit, however.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Battle Area:'
	R
	'The size of a battlefield. Only applies when you’re'
	R
	'fighting in a city or dungeon rather than a plain.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'The size limits the number of troops that can fight'
	R
	'at once. For example, a unit of 2000 troops can only'
	R
	'attack with 500 troops if the battle area is 500.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Defense Effects:'
	R
	'If you’re defending and choose to fight in the city,'
	R
	'you get an advantage based on that city’s defense.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Turn Order:'
	R
	'Generally, the less troops a unit has, the sooner'
	R
	'they move.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Front Line and Back Line'
	R
	'The first two units you selected for deployment are'
	R
	'in the front line and the other two are in the back.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Only units in the front line can make direct'
	R
	'attacks. Units in the back are limited to ranged'
	R
	'attacks. Units can’t switch lines during battle.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Warrior Unit: Can only attack in the front line.'
	R
	'Bow Unit: Can attack in either line.'
	R
	'Magic Unit: Can attack in either line.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Unit Annihilation:'
	R
	'When a general’s HP hits 0, the general’s entire'
	R
	'unit is annihilated.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_006d1:
	ZH 1:
	'You can perform all of the following actions once'
	R
	'per Rance Army Phase.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Subordinates Command:'
	R
	'You can either replenish a large number of one'
	R
	'unit’s troops or increase a unit’s max troops.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Subordinates Command:'
	R
	'On top of performing one of the previous two'
	R
	'actions, you may also talk to a subordinate.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Harem Command:'
	R
	'Calls a girl from Rance’s harem to have sex.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Merchant Command:'
	R
	'Calls the merchant Pluepet for shopping.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'War:'
	R
	'You can attack a territory that’s connected to one'
	R
	'of your own by a path.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'You can attack as many times as you want until'
	R
	'either you’ve conquered a territory or you’ve run'
	R
	'out of units to use.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Territory Command:'
	R
	'Choices in territories both under or not under your'
	R
	'control. You can do one of the following:'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Exclusive Location: Go somewhere unique to an area.'
	R
	'Temporary Levy: Collect money in your territory.'
	R
	'Bolster Defense: Raise defense of your territory.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Dungeon Command:'
	R
	'Search dungeons and specific buildings connected to'
	R
	'your territories.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_007e3:
	ZH 1:
	'This game is about taking the role of Rance in his'
	R
	'struggle to take over the world.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'A week passes in-game every turn. Each turn is made'
	R
	'up of multiple phases. The phase order is:'
	R
	'Rance Army Phase > Enemy Phases > Turn End'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_0081b:
	ZH 1:
	'A unit is made up of a general and the troops under'
	R
	'them. The unit’s maximum number of troops is based'
	R
	'on the general’s commanding ability.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'At the start of a turn, if a unit has less than its'
	R
	'maximum number of troops, it will restore some'
	R
	'troops.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'You may also restore a large number of troops to one'
	R
	'unit by selecting Replenish Troops on the'
	R
	'Subordinates screen, but this method costs money.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'A unit can fight in only one battle per turn.'
	R
	'If a unit acts during the Rance Army phase, it can’t'
	R
	'act during the enemy faction phases.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
*L_00894:
	ZH 1:
	'While different from units, ninjas can also only act'
	R
	'once per turn. They can collect enemy information'
	R
	'and sabotage enemy nations.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'It’s also possible for them to be captured, though,'
	R
	'in which case you’ll lose them forever.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'You can always safely scout with a ninja when the'
	R
	'enemy is attacking you, however.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0024e:
