*L_00cc6:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Payoooon.'
	R
	'　　　  You can hear me but not see me.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「This is Tori, Alicesoft’s filthy erotic'
	R
	'     writer.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Yukichi「Caw caw.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Hey, shut up, bird. What will... should be'
	R
	'     coming after Kichikuou Rance is a game called'
	R
	'     Ikenai Katsumi Sensei.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Yukichi「Caw!!」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Worried about when it will... should be coming'
	R
	'     out?'
	R
	'     Quiet, bird.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Uh～～～... Well...」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「The protagonist, Dr. Katsumi, is the same Dr.'
	R
	'     Katsumi from DPS’s Ikenai Naika Kenshin.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Dr. Katsumi’s audacious life has been made into'
	R
	'     a game.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「There’s no goal, just play a game as Dr.'
	R
	'     Katsumi. You could say it’s an adventure game,'
	R
	'     I guess??」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「There are men with suits, glasses and parted'
	R
	'     hair in it, something I’m personally'
	R
	'     interested in.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Also, don’t know how many people would know'
	R
	'     about this since the game is out of print, but'
	R
	'     there’s a Dr. Stop character...」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Dr. Kira makes an appearance.'
	R
	'　　　  Wow.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「The artist is Kazuma G Version, artist for'
	R
	'     Elven Bride.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Also, the CGs are using an incredible 60000'
	R
	'     colors. As such, it will be a bit demanding'
	R
	'     when it comes to specs.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「First, be able to run Windows 95.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Next, have a computer that displays 800 x 600'
	R
	'     pixels and over 60000 colors, as well as a'
	R
	'     sufficient monitor.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「It’s recommended your CPU be a 100 MHz Pentium'
	R
	'     or greater, and you have 16MB of memory or'
	R
	'     greater.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「If your little Pentiums and memories are good'
	R
	'     enough, you’ll have a pleasant gaming'
	R
	'     experience.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Also... It’ll take a lot of hard disk space...」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「I can’t say how much yet, but...'
	R
	'　　　  It’ll be a lot, in any case.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Yukichi「Caaaaaaw!!」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「I’ll eat you, bird.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Also, there’s 4 BMP images of sample CGs'
	R
	'     included on the Kichikuou CD.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Only look at them if you’re capable of'
	R
	'     displaying 60000 colors.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「They’re in the folder named Katsumi on the'
	R
	'     Kichikuou CD, please take a look.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Now, until we meet again.'
	R
	'　　　  Ngah, gggh.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Yukichi「Caaaaw.」'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Tori「Munch.」'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0007f:
*L_00f49:
	ZH 1:
	'Alicesoft provides numerous services on their'
	R
	'internet homepage.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Everyone, even people that don’t have a computer,'
	R
	'should know about the internet.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Alicesoft games and goods are sold on the homepage,'
	R
	'and there’s user support too.'
	R
	'There’s even 4-panel manga by Hide-SAN.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Then there’s the user club restricted to members'
	R
	'only, \"Alice’s Villa\".'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Here you can get info faster than from any magazine,'
	R
	'as well a download service for games only members'
	R
	'can play.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'If you’re interested, please fill out the club'
	R
	'membership registration and use your ID and password'
	R
	'to access the club bulletin.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'...'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'The URL is...'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'http//alicesoft.co.jp'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Oh, and we started an e-mail address called'
	R
	'\"Japan Alice Party\".'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'It sends out announcements that our homepage has'
	R
	'updated.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'You can register to receive e-mails on our homepage.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Sign up, everyone.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'That’s all about the internet.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0007f:
*L_0106d:
	ZH 1:
	'Hi, this is Arunaru, the translator. This section'
	R
	'used to be about Xspec, something that measures your'
	R
	'PC’s performance.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'But since it’s almost 20 years from this game’s'
	R
	'original release now, you’re probably using a PC'
	R
	'that can run this game.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'So instead I’ll talk a bit about this game itself.'
	R
	'A lot goes around about this game that isn’t'
	R
	'necessarily accurate.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Kichikuou Rance was at first being developed as'
	R
	'Rance 5, but at some point during development it was'
	R
	'decided it would be a \"What if?\" game.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'It takes place in an alternate timeline from the'
	R
	'main series splitting off after Rance 4.2.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'The goal of the developers was to fit in every idea'
	R
	'they thought of for the series but hadn’t yet used'
	R
	'all in one game. It came out in December, 1996.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'The result was hugely successful for an eroge, kept'
	R
	'selling for around a decade after its release and'
	R
	'kept a place in eroge magazine rankings for years.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Total sales are hard to find but it sold about 75000'
	R
	'copies by the end of 1997 and presumably over 100000'
	R
	'copies in total. It’s been freeware since 2006.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'While future Rance games went a different route'
	R
	'from this game, they’ve been highly influenced by'
	R
	'it and frequently reintroduce characters and events.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'Another interesting tidbit about this game is that'
	R
	'it was actually minimally debugged and proofread due'
	R
	'to the random nature of it all.'
	\L_018fb:
	ZH 1:
	'I fixed a number of the bugs and left others because'
	R
	'you can do some fun stuff. The most important thing'
	R
	'is that all the items do what they claim now.'
	\L_018fb:
	@L_0007f:
	]
	\L_01908:
	@L_0007f:
